Subject: Leak on 2-RV-102 elbow - line isolated, clamp fitted
Message-ID: <6fbf5df53e46c8c1282c154b@qscp.example.invalid>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

Dear Douglas,

A pinhole leak was identified at a 90° elbow on line 2-RV-102 within the ATU-100. As there was no CML at this specific elbow location, the leak was not predicted by current data. The line has been isolated and a temporary clamp fitted to maintain integrity.

This line is a Class 1 regenerator overhead service with a t-min of 2.79 mm. We need to review the existing QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 0 to determine if additional monitoring locations are required for this circuit to prevent future loss of containment.

Regards,  Gordon Lisle Douglas Ferreira

